Use `@core/text` to ask questions about a String. Select the functions you
need from the package. For example, you might want to recognise template
files by their names:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    @core/text length, is_empty, contains, starts_with, ends_with

    file_name = "report.mtf"
    size = length(file_name)
    blank = is_empty(file_name)
    has_dot = contains(file_name, ".")
    hidden = starts_with(file_name, ".")
    template_file = ends_with(file_name, ".mtf")
]

`length` counts Unicode scalar values and returns an I32. Here `size` holds
10. The other functions return a Bool. The name contains a dot and ends in
`.mtf`, so `has_dot` and `template_file` are true. The name has text and
starts with a letter, so `blank` and `hidden` are false.

Pass arguments by position. The Advanced view describes compile-time
evaluation and target support.
